{title: What Wondrous Love Is This}
{artist: American folk hymn}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (What_Wondrous_Love_Is_This-Wondrous_Love_Southern_Harmony)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]What [Am]wondrous love [A7]is [Dm]this,
[Am]O my [Dm]soul, O [F]my [C]soul!
[F]What wondrous love is [Dm]this,
[A7]O [Am]my [Dm]soul!
[C]What [F]won[C]drous [F]love is [Dm]this
[Dm]That [Am]caused the Lord of [Dm]bliss
[Dm]To [Am]bear the dread[A7]ful [Dm]curse
[Am]For my [Dm]soul, for [F]my [C]soul,
[F]To bear the dreadful [Dm]curse
[A7]For [Am]my [Dm]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]When [Am]I was sin[A7]king [Dm]down,
[Am]Sinking [Dm]down, sin[F]king [C]down,
[F]When I was sinking [Dm]down,
[A7]Sin[Am]king [Dm]down,
[C]When [F]I [C]was [F]sinking [Dm]down
[Dm]Be[Am]neath God’s righteous [Dm]frown,
[Dm]Christ [Am]laid aside [A7]His [Dm]crown
[Am]For my [Dm]soul, for [F]my [C]soul,
[F]Christ laid aside His [Dm]crown
[A7]For [Am]my [Dm]soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Ye [Am]wingèd se[A7]raphs [Dm]fly,
[Am]Bear the [Dm]news, bear [F]the [C]news!
[F]Ye wingèd seraphs [Dm]fly,
[A7]Bear [Am]the [Dm]news!
[C]Ye [F]win[C]gèd [F]seraphs [Dm]fly,
[Dm]Like [Am]comets through the [Dm]sky,
[Dm]Fill [Am]vast eter[A7]ni[Dm]ty
[Am]With the [Dm]news, with [F]the [C]news!
[F]Fill vast eterni[Dm]ty
[A7]With [Am]the [Dm]news!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]To [Am]God and to [A7]the [Dm]Lamb,
[Am]I will [Dm]sing, I [F]will [C]sing;
[F]To God and to the [Dm]Lamb,
[A7]I [Am]will [Dm]sing.
[C]To [F]God [C]and [F]to the [Dm]Lamb
[Dm]Who [Am]is the great I [Dm]Am;
[Dm]While [Am]millions join [A7]the [Dm]theme,
[Am]I will [Dm]sing, I [F]will [C]sing;
[F]While millions join the [Dm]theme,
[A7]I [Am]will [Dm]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm]Ye [Am]friends of Zi[A7]on’s [Dm]king,
[Am]Join His [Dm]praise, join [F]His [C]praise;
[F]Ye friends of Zion’s [Dm]king,
[A7]Join [Am]His [Dm]praise;
[C]Ye [F]friends [C]of [F]Zion’s [Dm]king,
[Dm]With [Am]hearts and voices [Dm]sing,
[Dm]And [Am]strike each tune[A7]ful [Dm]string
[Am]In His [Dm]praise, in [F]His [C]praise!
[F]And strike each tuneful [Dm]string
[A7]In [Am]His [Dm]praise!
{end_of_verse}
